<title>USA: Texas Instruments Q3 net declines.</title>
<headline>Texas Instruments Q3 net declines.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr     loss    $0.78	  profit  $1.48</p>
<p> Net     loss    148,000	profit  289,000</p>
<p> Revs		2,841,000		3,425,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  189,700		  195,100</p>
<p>	  9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.48		    $4.13</p>
<p> Net		 91,000		   797,000</p>
<p> Revs		8,761,000		9,525,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  191,800		  193,300</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) Full company name is Texas Instruments Inc</p>
<p>NOTE: Third quarter and the first nine months 1996 net income included a $192 millon in-process research and development charge. The company also said it was offering enchanced voluntary early retirement fo about 5,300 U.S. based employees, in light of the current market environment.</p>
